# The cohort's descriptor map (the Pulumi stack's `nodes` output, saved as
# nodes/nodes.json), the founding bootnode set beside it, and the per-node
# `<node>.init-config.toml` records of what `configure` POSTed — runtime
# output (live IPs, regenerated each deploy, gone with the stack), never
# committed. Everything else in a network directory is its committable
# identity.
*/nodes/

# Throwaway foundings (the recipe is the devnet runbook,
# https://github.com/SeismicSystems/deploy/blob/main/tee/docs/runbook-devnet.md):
# the whole directory is ignored, so a scratch cohort can be founded, torn
# down, and deleted without touching git. A network that matters gets an unprefixed
# directory — its identity is committed.
tmp-*/
